+## P-01: Progress framework substitutions
+
+Source: pinned [Progress parts](https://github.com/mui/base-ui/tree/47b40521eab921c2756bf9bdb0b0f07fbfdb8c8c/packages/react/src/progress) and [useRegisteredLabelId](https://github.com/mui/base-ui/blob/47b40521eab921c2756bf9bdb0b0f07fbfdb8c8c/packages/react/src/utils/useRegisteredLabelId.ts). Svelte uses native class, string CSS, snippets, bindings/attachments and native events within the accepted five API substitutions in T-01; initially undefined refs follow A-01. Typed context exposes derived values, Svelte-stable IDs preserve generated relationships, and post-mount label registration preserves SSR omission followed by hydration association. React component namespace types become named part Props/State; ProgressStatus, Progress.Status and subpath Status remain public. Root's hidden presentation x and Value's default/child output are explicitly retained through replacement snippets.
+
+Rationale: implement the actual pinned contracts with a private Progress dependency closure; no shared helper or Input changes and no opportunistic correction of reversed/nonfinite bound arithmetic. The [compatibility record](../parity/progress/compatibility.md), [feature documentation](progress.md) and [dedicated assertion record](../parity/progress/README.md) distinguish 20 passing ordinary declarations at the secured component checkpoint, seven parameterized variants, full conformance and supplemental evidence. Shared aggregate credits remain unchanged. Decision status: proposed in [PR #28](https://github.com/sveltery/base/pull/28), within the accepted framework baseline; no additional behavioral deviation approval or complete assistive-technology/whole-library parity is claimed. The complete integrated head requires full tests, paired secured browsers, public consumers, independent review and configured automatic review before merge.
